  "notes": "Hardened Sprint 156 Task 10 spawn-time file lock by closing a real lock-leak bug in the docker backend. Baseline state: src/core/file-lock.ts already exported the full .spawnlock API (SpawnLockInfo, SpawnLockError, acquireSpawnLock/Locks with batch rollback, releaseSpawnLock/Locks, releaseAllSpawnLocks); 18-case tests/core/file-lock-runtime.test.ts was green; DockerSpawnBackend.spawn() acquired locks via acquireSpawnTimeLocks() and released them on container exit / kill() / image-not-found. Gap identified: between the lock acquisition and the successful handoff to monitorContainer(), several failure paths could leak locks: (a) the `docker run` non-zero status path silently wrote a .timeout marker and returned without releasing, permanently blocking any retry / fix worker spawned for the same file scope (transient docker errors became hard locks); (b) any throw from the WSL2 check / writeFileSync(promptHostPath) / writeFileSync(scriptHostPath) / spawnSync wrapper would leak in the same way. Fix: split spawn() into a thin acquire-locks + try/catch wrapper that delegates the body to a new private runSpawn(); the catch arm calls releaseAllSpawnLocks(dir, taskId) before rethrowing. The non-zero-status early-return path is augmented with an explicit releaseAllSpawnLocks call so the silent-return semantics are preserved while still freeing the locks. The image-not-found path now simply throws (catch arm handles the release). Added regression test (`cleanup-on-failure: releaseAllSpawnLocks unblocks a different task after a simulated failure`) — confirms that after a simulated post-acquire failure, a different task (e.g. the fix worker) can claim the same files. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` → 0 errors. `npx vitest run` on 4 relevant suites (file-lock, file-lock-runtime, unit/spawn-backend-docker, orchestra/tmpfile-preservation) → 59/59 pass (was 58/58 before the regression test was added). ANCHOR compliance: no npm run build, no npm install, no project-wide tsc/vitest. ADR-001/002: ESM .js suffixes preserved. ADR-008: file-lock under core, docker backend under orchestra — import direction unchanged. ADR-006/007 (spawnSync security): no new spawn signatures introduced. ADR-037 RBAC: worker stayed within declared scope (src/core/, src/orchestra/, tests/core/ — only the two new modifications are in src/orchestra/spawn-backend-docker.ts and tests/core/file-lock-runtime.test.ts; src/core/file-lock.ts untouched in this fix since the API contract was already correct).",
